***************************************************************** 3034 1451
       Nuclear Model Calculation with CCONE code /7/              3034 1451
***************************************************************** 3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE calculation             3034 1451
  1) Optical model                                                3034 1451
    * coupled channels calculation                                3034 1451
      coupled levels: 0,5 (see Table 1)                           3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
    * optical model potential                                     3034 1451
      neutron  omp: Kunieda,S. et al./9/ (+)                      3034 1451
      proton   omp: Koning,A.J. and Delaroche,J.P./10/            3034 1451
      deuteron omp: Lohr,J.M. and Haeberli,W./11/                 3034 1451
      triton   omp: Becchetti Jr.,F.D. and Greenlees,G.W./12/     3034 1451
      He3      omp: Becchetti Jr.,F.D. and Greenlees,G.W./12/     3034 1451
      alpha    omp: Huizenga,J.R. and Igo,G./13/                  3034 1451
      (+) omp parameters were modified.                           3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
  2) Two-component exciton model/14/                              3034 1451
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/15/            3034 1451
      was used.                                                   3034 1451
    * Gamma emission channel/16/ was added to simulate direct     3034 1451
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            3034 1451
    * Width fluctuation correction/17/ was applied.               3034 1451
    * Neutron, proton, deuteron, triton, He3, alpha and gamma     3034 1451
      decay channel were taken into account.                      3034 1451
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       3034 1451
      optical model calculation.                                  3034 1451
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 1.         3034 1451
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 3034 1451
      model were used with shell energy correction/18/.           3034 1451
      Parameters are shown in Table 2.                            3034 1451
    * Gamma-ray strength function of standard Lorentzian form     3034 1451
      was used for E1 transition.                                 3034 1451
      For M1 and E2 transitions the standard Lorentzian form was  3034 1451
      adopted. The prameters are shown in Table 3.                3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
